In ancient times, Gybolg was used by the fierce dog warrior, [[Cú Chulainn]]. [[Scarlet Byrne]] theorized that Cú Chulainn had to defeat a water Titan or clear a water trap in order to find his Gybolg's [[Amulet]]. His Amulet was eventually left in the [[Newgrange Passage Tomb]] in Ireland. {{source|Home Turf}}

Years later, Scarlet, with the help of Dante´s team, managed to locate and bond with this Titan. Gybolg was then invoked to fight alongside Dante's team aginst [[Klaus|Klaus']] [[Suits]] and defeat one of their [[Bonelasher]] Titans. {{Source|Home Turf}}

Scarlet invoked Gybolg after she was ambushed by [[Firbolg]] the fierce giant whilst searching for [[Tír na nÓg]], the magical floating castle. After enduring some hits, Gybolg was able to demobilize Firbolg and defeat him. {{source|Back Home}}
